### Trade Gateway — CUSTOMS quantity endpoints (Local Development environment)

@host = http://localhost:5000
@scope = trade-gateway-resource-srv/access

### Token — customs quantity reader (READ on /customs/** only)
# @name customsToken
POST {{host}}/local/cognito/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

scope={{scope}}&sub=test-customs-quantity-reader

### Token — customs quantity manager (READ + WRITE on /customs/**)
# @name customsManagerToken
POST {{host}}/local/cognito/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

scope={{scope}}&sub=test-customs-quantity-manager

### Token — CHED reader (used here only to prove the /customs/** boundary)
# @name chedToken
POST {{host}}/local/cognito/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

scope={{scope}}&sub=test-ched-reader

###############################################################################
# CUSTOMS — quantity management
#
# Calls the customs TracesNT account (TracesNt:Credentials:Customs), not the
# default one, and needs TracesNt:CustomsOfficeReferenceNumber set or the app
# will not start. Both endpoints are the same upstream operation: the ledger
# read sends QuantityManagementIndication "0", the reservation sends "1" and
# mutates state in TracesNT.
###############################################################################

@chedId = CHEDP.XI.2026.0000686
@mrn = 26GB0012345678901

### Get the quantity ledger for a CHED
# 200 with available[] and allocations{reserved[],consumed[]}.
# Each allocation carries declarationReference {type,value} — filter on BOTH
# fields to narrow to one declaration; an LRN can carry the same value as an MRN.
GET {{host}}/customs/cheds/{{chedId}}/quantities
Accept: application/vnd.defra.trade.ched-quantities.v1+json
Accept-Language: en
Authorization: Bearer {{customsToken.response.body.access_token}}

### Unknown CHED returns 404
# TracesNT reports it as a response carrying no certificate rather than a fault, so this is
# the one not-found signal available. An actual upstream fault is a 502 instead — the port's
# single untyped fault says nothing, so it never becomes a 404.
GET {{host}}/customs/cheds/CHEDA.GB.2026.9999999/quantities
Accept-Language: en
Authorization: Bearer {{customsToken.response.body.access_token}}

### A CHED reader gets 403 on /customs/** — proves the prefix decision
# customs/ is a sibling of certificates/, so the ched-reader grant on
# /certificates/cheds/** cannot reach customs quantity data.
GET {{host}}/customs/cheds/{{chedId}}/quantities
Accept-Language: en
Authorization: Bearer {{chedToken.response.body.access_token}}

### A customs reader gets 403 on /certificates/** — the boundary holds both ways
GET {{host}}/certificates/cheds/CHEDA.XI.2026.0000063
Accept-Language: en
Authorization: Bearer {{customsToken.response.body.access_token}}

###############################################################################
# CUSTOMS — reserving quantity against a declaration
#
# PUT is deliberate: the body states the declaration's whole position against the
# CHED, so re-sending it with different numbers replaces the previous hold rather
# than adding to it. The response is narrowed to this declaration, unlike the
# ledger above which reports the CHED's whole position.
###############################################################################

### Reserve against a declaration
# 200 with reserved[] and consumed[] for this MRN only.
# goodsItemNumber, certificateLineNumber and classCode are required on every item. Weight and
# volume are independent — send either or both, but a quantity without its unit of measure is a
# 400, never a silent default (TracesNT would assume tonnes).
PUT {{host}}/customs/cheds/{{chedId}}/declarations/{{mrn}}/reservation
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/vnd.defra.trade.ched-reservation.v1+json
Accept-Language: en
Authorization: Bearer {{customsManagerToken.response.body.access_token}}

{
  "items": [
    {
      "goodsItemNumber": 1,
      "certificateLineNumber": 1,
      "classCode": "04071100",
      "netWeightQuantity": 2000,
      "netWeightUnitOfMeasure": "GRM"
    }
  ]
}


### Refused by TracesNT returns 409 with the decoded reason
# Ask for more than the CHED has left — expect failureReason {"code":"05","description":
# "Quantities insufficient"} plus a failedItem extension with goodsItemNumber and
# documentLineItemNumber. A code outside the gateway's table comes back as code null with
# "Unrecognised reservation failure reason": the raw element is free text and is logged,
# never echoed (ADR-0002 §4).
PUT {{host}}/customs/cheds/{{chedId}}/declarations/{{mrn}}/reservation
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en
Authorization: Bearer {{customsManagerToken.response.body.access_token}}

{
  "items": [
    {
      "goodsItemNumber": 1,
      "certificateLineNumber": 1,
      "classCode": "1522000001",
      "netWeightQuantity": 99999999,
      "netWeightUnitOfMeasure": "KGM"
    }
  ]
}

### Empty items returns 400 — a reservation of nothing is not a way to release a hold
PUT {{host}}/customs/cheds/{{chedId}}/declarations/{{mrn}}/reservation
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en
Authorization: Bearer {{customsManagerToken.response.body.access_token}}

{
  "items": []
}

### Quantity without a unit of measure returns 400
# Not a default: TracesNT would read the missing unit as tonnes.
PUT {{host}}/customs/cheds/{{chedId}}/declarations/{{mrn}}/reservation
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en
Authorization: Bearer {{customsManagerToken.response.body.access_token}}

{
  "items": [
    {
      "goodsItemNumber": 1,
      "certificateLineNumber": 1,
      "classCode": "1522000001",
      "netWeightQuantity": 300
    }
  ]
}

### Weight AND volume on one item — allowed, not mutually exclusive
# The CERTEX guidelines §3.2 say quantity management uses Net mass (18 01 001 000) "and/or"
# Supplementary Unit (18 02 001 000). The XSD agrees: four independent optional elements with no
# choice construct, unlike CustomsDeclarationReferenceNumber where MRN/LRN generated one.
# A domain business rule can still refuse the combination — that arrives as a 409, not a 400.
PUT {{host}}/customs/cheds/{{chedId}}/declarations/{{mrn}}/reservation
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en
Authorization: Bearer {{customsManagerToken.response.body.access_token}}

{
  "items": [
    {
      "goodsItemNumber": 1,
      "certificateLineNumber": 1,
      "classCode": "1522000001",
      "netWeightQuantity": 100,
      "netWeightUnitOfMeasure": "KGM",
      "netVolumeQuantity": 2,
      "netVolumeUnitOfMeasure": "MTQ"
    }
  ]
}

### Unrecognised unit of measure returns 400
# UN/ECE Recommendation 20 codes only — "KILOS" is not one, and is rejected rather than
# falling back to the enum's first member (TNE).
PUT {{host}}/customs/cheds/{{chedId}}/declarations/{{mrn}}/reservation
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en
Authorization: Bearer {{customsManagerToken.response.body.access_token}}

{
  "items": [
    {
      "goodsItemNumber": 1,
      "certificateLineNumber": 1,
      "classCode": "1522000001",
      "netWeightQuantity": 300,
      "netWeightUnitOfMeasure": "KILOS"
    }
  ]
}

### Missing a required item field returns 400
# TracesNT's schema requires goodsItemNumber, certificateLineNumber and classCode, and a missing one
# is left out of the request rather than sent empty — so without the check the call fails upstream as
# a SAXException and returns a 500. Drop any of the three from this body to see it reported.
PUT {{host}}/customs/cheds/{{chedId}}/declarations/{{mrn}}/reservation
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en
Authorization: Bearer {{customsManagerToken.response.body.access_token}}

{
  "items": [
    {
      "certificateLineNumber": 1,
      "netWeightQuantity": 300,
      "netWeightUnitOfMeasure": "KGM"
    }
  ]
}

### Unknown CHED returns 404, same signal as the ledger read
PUT {{host}}/customs/cheds/CHEDA.GB.2026.9999999/declarations/{{mrn}}/reservation
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en
Authorization: Bearer {{customsManagerToken.response.body.access_token}}

{
  "items": [
    {
      "goodsItemNumber": 1,
      "certificateLineNumber": 1,
      "classCode": "1522000001",
      "netWeightQuantity": 300,
      "netWeightUnitOfMeasure": "KGM"
    }
  ]
}

### The read-only customs principal gets 403 — READ does not imply WRITE
# Same /customs/** resource as the ledger GET it is allowed to call; only the action differs.
PUT {{host}}/customs/cheds/{{chedId}}/declarations/{{mrn}}/reservation
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en
Authorization: Bearer {{customsToken.response.body.access_token}}

{
  "items": [
    {
      "goodsItemNumber": 1,
      "certificateLineNumber": 1,
      "classCode": "1522000001",
      "netWeightQuantity": 300,
      "netWeightUnitOfMeasure": "KGM"
    }
  ]
}

### A CHED reader gets 403 on the reservation too
PUT {{host}}/customs/cheds/{{chedId}}/declarations/{{mrn}}/reservation
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en
Authorization: Bearer {{chedToken.response.body.access_token}}

{
  "items": [
    {
      "goodsItemNumber": 1,
      "certificateLineNumber": 1,
      "classCode": "1522000001",
      "netWeightQuantity": 300,
      "netWeightUnitOfMeasure": "KGM"
    }
  ]
}

### The manager can still read the ledger — WRITE grants carry READ on /customs/**
GET {{host}}/customs/cheds/{{chedId}}/quantities
Accept-Language: en
Authorization: Bearer {{customsManagerToken.response.body.access_token}}
